Mortar's Vite plugin. Add it next to `@solidjs/vite-plugin`:

```ts
import { mortarKit } from '@mortar-kit/admin/vite';
import midnight from '@mortar-kit/theme-midnight';

export default defineConfig({ plugins: [solid({ ... }), mortarKit({ theme: midnight })] });
```

Where documents live: raw data by collection name and slug. Implement it
to keep content anywhere (files, a database, an API). Deliberately dumb;
`createContent` applies every rule.

examples:
```ts
export const posts = defineCollection({
  name: 'posts',
  label: 'Posts',
  fields: { title: fields.text({ label: 'Title', required: true }), date: fields.date({ label: 'Date' }) },
  body: true,
  sort: { field: 'date', order: 'desc' },
});
```
